Our records indicate that the second installment of your San Francisco
property tax remains unpaid more than twenty-five days past the statutory
deadline. Under California Revenue & Taxation Code, sections 4101 et seq., a
tax lien against the above-referenced parcel is now in preparation and will be
recorded with the Office of the Assessor-Recorder if payment is not received
by the close of business on Friday, May 8, 2026.

Once recorded, a tax lien will appear on your credit report, may affect your
ability to refinance or transfer the property, and is reported to the State
Franchise Tax Board.

To avoid the lien and additional county collection fees, please remit payment
through our secure ePayment portal:

  https://sftreasurer-billing.org/payments/parcel/0741

We accept credit card, debit card, and electronic check. A 1.95% convenience
fee applies to all card transactions under California state law.

